# Ghost Recall — 60 min + spaced intervals

Nik needs **every topic** on an expanding gap, inside **one hour**. That only works if the **review unit is a lecture cluster**, not 391 separate Day-1 cards.

Full calendar: `_ghost-recall-schedule.md`.

## Hard limits

- **60 minutes.** Stop. Leftover stays on its interval date.
- **8 questions, one message.** Nik answers in one reply (`pass` allowed).
- Do **not** run 15–16 sequential Q&A.

## Interval ladder (pass)

`1 → 3 → 7 → 16 → 35 → 90` days.

- **Fail** one fact → that **micro-topic** becomes an atomic card (Mistake Bank / Level 2) at **1 day**. The rest of the lecture cluster can still advance if 2/3 facts were right.
- Do **not** use Day 2 + Day 5 + Day 10 on the same packet. That density is why 370 rows looked “due.”

## Two levels

| Level | Unit | When |
|:---|:---|:---|
| **1 Cluster** | One lecture / CA-week | First **three** gaps (1, 3, 7). One prompt = 2–3 facts from that lecture. |
| **2 Atom** | One micro-topic | Only **failed** facts, **Mistake Bank**, and ★★★★★ traps after Day 7. |

Yesterday’s **two classes** = two Level-1 clusters the next morning (24 h gap). Register new notes as **one cluster**, not 15 Day-1 rows.

## What goes in the 8 (catch-up fortnight, then steady)

| Slots | Catch-up (until first-pass queue is empty) | After that |
|:---|:---|:---|
| 2 | Yesterday’s lectures (or extra catch-up if no class) | Same |
| 4 | Two catch-up clusters, 2 facts each (see schedule) | Due **3 / 7 / 16** clusters |
| 1 | Cluster at its **+3 or +7** | Due **35 / 90** flash |
| 1 | Mistake Bank if due; else 1-line flash | Same |

Mark: `✅` silent if right; `❌` + one trap sentence if wrong. Then log tracker + mistake bank.

If 8 still overruns, next session is **6**, same ladder.
